>> servings: 4
>> source: https://www.nemlig.com/opskrifter/quesadillas-kylling-98004516

Cut the @chicken breast{400%g} into thin slices.

Peel and chop the @red onion{1}.

Heat a #frying pan{} over medium heat with a little @neutral oil{}.

Brown the chicken and add the @fajita mix{1%package}. Stir until the chicken is well browned and golden.

Add the red onion and fry for another ~soften{2%minutes}.

Add the @tomato paste{2%tbsp} and let it fry for ~cook{2%minutes}.

If the @spinach{200%g} has not been washed, rinse it in a colander under cold water and shake dry.

Turn off the heat and stir the @creme fraiche{0.75%dl} into the chicken until creamy. Add the spinach and let it wilt in the warm chicken, covering with a lid if needed.

Season with @salt{} and @pepper{}.

Tip the filling into a bowl and wipe the pan clean; you will need it again shortly.

Divide the chicken and @grated cheese{140%g} over half of each @tortilla{8}, then fold them in half.

Place the folded tortillas in the same pan; any creamy residue from the chicken is fine.

Fry them for ~golden{3%minutes} on each side until golden and the cheese has melted.

Continue until all the tortillas are used.

Cut the quesadillas into smaller triangles.

Slice the @avocado{2}. Rinse and finely slice the @spring onion{0.5}.

Cut the @lime{1} into wedges.

Serve the warm quesadillas with a spoonful of cold @creme fraiche{1.25%dl}, spring onion, avocado and lime wedges.
